From ce6201d319baf7443022fc82ba99e72e60d237a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:48:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: when HDR goes over the tunnel as YCbCr 4:2:2
 at 12 bits, and why not (the rule only)

The kernel side (DVBRIDGE_HDR10_TUNNEL_LAB, linux-9932 to 9934) sends HDR as
YCbCr 4:2:2 at 12 bits packed in the RGB 8 bpc tunnel, for 2160p50 and 2160p60 on
i915 and on amdgpu DCN 3.1 and 3.1.5, where HDMI 2.0 does not carry RGB at 10
bits and the ordinary output is YCbCr 4:2:0 at 10 bits or RGB at 8. This is
Kodi's decision of when to ask for it, and nothing else of it yet:

- HDR10Tunnel.h: Decide() over the setting, the driver (kernel backend with the
  property), the link (HDMI over TMDS), the EDID (YCbCr 4:2:2 and an HDR block),
  the picture (HDR), native Dolby Vision (the other tunnel), the mode (3840x2160
  at 50 or 60 Hz) and what the ordinary output would send (DVBRIDGE_LINK_FORMAT:
  RGB at 8 bits or 4:2:0 only; the driver's own 4:2:2, RGB at 10 or more, or a
  format not known are "no": fail closed), with a short code for each reason.
- EdidYcbcr422.h and CDisplayInfo::SupportsYCbCr422(): the capability bit of the
  CTA-861 blocks as the kernel reads it (a block with a wrong checksum counts for
  nothing).

Nothing calls the rule yet: the picture for the tunnel is made by the engine of
native Dolby Vision, which takes Dolby Vision streams only (DVBRIDGE::Eligible()).
Host test: 51271 checks, and three mutations of the headers that it catches.
---
 xbmc/utils/DisplayInfo.cpp       |   3 +
 xbmc/utils/DisplayInfo.h         |   4 +
 xbmc/utils/EdidYcbcr422.h        |  44 ++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10Tunnel.h | 133 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 184 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/utils/EdidYcbcr422.h
 create mode 100644 xbmc/windowing/gbm/HDR10Tunnel.h

diff --git a/xbmc/utils/DisplayInfo.cpp b/xbmc/utils/DisplayInfo.cpp
index bfb6a9b..e3be0ff 100644
